{
  "scenarioVersion": 2,
  "meta": {
    "name": "Bus-stop emergence — pedestrian from in front of a dwelling bus",
    "description": "A bus dwells at a kerbside stop with its doors open; a passenger who has just got off walks round the front of it and into the carriageway. The anchor requires a real `bus_stop` on the reference path, so the scenario lands where buses actually stop rather than at an arbitrary kerb. The bus itself is an L3 prop: it is stationary for the whole clip, and the engine's pairwise TTC circumscribes both footprints without regard to lanes, so a 12 m *actor* parked 3 m to the ego's side pins the episode min-TTC at zero and takes the metric away from the pedestrian (measured — see the campaign report). The cost of that choice is that `doors.left` is not settable on a prop; the open-doors cue is carried as a prop extension until the engine treats parked actors as scenery. The `bus_stop` anchor feature is declared but cosmetic: on all five maps the catalog anchors bus stops onto the sidewalk or shoulder lane beside the carriageway, and the matcher only searches point features lying on the driving reference path, so the clause can never bind. Required, it returns zero sites on every map; cosmetic, it records the intent and the corridor clauses carry the match.",
    "createdAt": "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z",
    "modifiedAt": "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z",
    "appVersion": "scen/0.0.1",
    "archetype": "C5.bus-stop-emergence",
    "tags": [
      "vru",
      "occlusion",
      "bus-stop",
      "transit",
      "prop-occluder",
      "campaign-occluded-pedestrian"
    ],
    "author": "agent/campaign-occluded-pedestrian",
    "negativeControl": false
  },
  "params": {
